      "writtenOn": "2023-01-24T21:57:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I understand that, but \"showing the device\" isn\u0027t what BT does, that\u0027s the Settings part.\nSo I would let Settings use this extra to show it or not but name it as what it really is in our codebase: a flag saying this device is a \"counterpart device\".\n\nFor example, say one day Settings decide to show both devices and their battery differ, `IS_HIDDEN_FROM_USER` wouldn\u0027t make sense in that case I think",
